TI  - EMS Federal and State Laws Affecting Tactical Medicine.
BTI - StatPearls
AB  - Serving as a specialized branch of emergency medical services (EMS) and a 
      subspecialty of Tactical Medicine, Tactical Emergency Medical Support (TEMS) has 
      the primary goal of providing medical care while in a tactical environment to 
      reduce physical and moral injury, preserve safety, and save lives while 
      accomplishing the primary objective or mission. By reducing risk, bodily harm, 
      and death to tactical team members, bystanders/civilians, and suspects, TEMS 
      members achieve this goal. TEMS-trained providers include EMTs, paramedics, 
      nurses, advanced practice providers, and physicians. They are frequently embedded 
      within a tactical team and have direct and indirect impacts on medical care, 
      primarily training team members how to perform buddy aid and occasionally 
      providing direct medical care during operations.
