TI  - Conducting fresh whole blood transfusion training.
PG  - S184-S190
LID - 10.1097/TA.0000000000002323 [doi]
AB  - Fresh whole blood is the optimal resuscitation fluid for casualties in 
      hemorrhagic shock according to the Committee on Tactical Combat Casualty Care and 
      has demonstrated to improve outcomes in severely wounded patients. Like all 
      medical interventions, fresh whole blood transfusions are not without risks, but 
      similarly can be mitigated through increased training to develop provider 
      knowledge and proficiency. To date, no literature has been published regarding 
      the proper technique to conduct fresh whole blood transfusion training. This 
      article provides a structured foundation to establish a standardized fresh whole 
      blood transfusion training program to increase skill and preparedness for fresh 
      whole blood protocol implementation. Using these techniques in a training 
      environment, providers will be able to provide optimal resuscitation in 
      hemorrhagic shock in austere environments.
