TI  - 2019 Recommended Limb Tourniquets in Tactical Combat Casualty Care.
PG  - 27-50
LID - HQDV-7SXN [pii]
LID - 10.55460/HQDV-7SXN [doi]
AB  - Military and civilian trauma can be distinctly different but the leading cause of 
      preventable trauma deaths in the prehospital environment, extremity hemorrhage, 
      does not discriminate. The current paper is the most comprehensive review of limb 
      tourniquets employable in the tactical combat casualty care environment and 
      provides the first update to the CoTCCC-recommended limb tourniquets since 2005. 
      This review also highlights the lack of unbiased data, official reporting 
      mechanisms, and official studies with established criteria for evaluating 
      tourniquets. Upon review of the data, the CoTCCC voted to update the 
      recommendations in April 2019.
CI  - 2019.
