TI  - Ethical considerations in embedding a surgeon in a military or civilian tactical 
      team.
PG  - 583-8
LID - 10.1017/S1049023X12001112 [doi]
AB  - Tactical emergency medical services (TEMS) bring immediate medical support to the 
      inner perimeter of special weapons and tactics team activations. While initially 
      envisioned as a role for an individual dually trained as a police officer and 
      paramedic, TEMS is increasingly undertaken by physicians and paramedics who are 
      not police officers. This report explores the ethical underpinnings of embedding 
      a surgeon within a military or civilian tactical team with regard to identity, 
      ethically acceptable actions, triage, responsibility set, training, 
      certification, and potential future refinements of the role of the tactical 
      police surgeon.
